    "intro_html":  "Peruvian roast chicken is famous for two things: a cumin and vinegar marinade that soaks in overnight, and the green sauce that shows up beside it. That sauce, aji verde, is where the whole plate turns from good to memorable. Cilantro, chile, garlic and a little mayonnaise blitzed until it looks like house paint and tastes like a secret. Thighs marinate, one pan roasts, rice underneath, sauce over the top. Each bowl runs \u003cstrong\u003e576 calories and 34 grams of protein\u003c/strong\u003e for about \u003cstrong\u003e$1.15\u003c/strong\u003e.",
